{"results":[{"url":"https://www.whitehouse.gov/mediabias/","final_url":"https://www.whitehouse.gov/mediabias/","title":"Media Offenders","description":"Explore the Media Bias Tracker that fact checks and holds Fake News accountable. False claims debunked, Hall of Shame for serial offenders, Leaderboard of networks ranked by Repeated Lies. Stay informed, stay accurate.","language":"en","text":"## Media Offenders\n\n## Misleading. Biased*.* *Exposed*.\n\n## media offender of the week:\n\n* **OUTLET**\n\n  CNN\n\n  **REPORTER**\n\n  Jonathan Reiner, Kate Bolduan\n\n  **CLAIM**\n\n  ### CNN Lies About President Trump’s Health\n\n  **CATEGORY**\n\n  Conspiracy Theories, Left-Wing Lunacy\n\n  **THE OFFENSE**\n\n  Dr. Jonathan Reiner joined Kate Bolduan on CNN’s morning show where they sowed doubt about his health: “The president has severe daytime somnolence. He falls asleep very often. He’s fallen asleep in the Oval Office on multiple occasions with people talking to him, in the cabinet room.”\n\n  **THE TRUTH**\n\n  This is a blatant lie founded upon cherry-picked screenshots of President Trump blinking or reading. This moronic conspiracy theory from a “medical expert” originated as a fringe talking point for chronically online leftists trying to save face after covering up Joe Biden’s cognitive decline for four years. President Trump just completed his physical and received a clean bill of health from one of the nation’s greatest doctors. Their claims are demonstrably false, and are a projection of their failure and shame.\n\n  **KEY POINTS**\n\n  • CNN platformed a charlatan posing as a medical expert to promulgate lies about President Trump’s health.\n\n  **SOURCES**\n\n## Offender Hall of Shame\n\nA record of the media’s false and misleading stories  \nflagged by The White House. Scroll for the Truth.\n\nreset results\n\nClaim\n\nPublication \n\nAll\nABC News Apple News Associated Press Axios Bloomberg Bloomberg Government CBS News CNN Daily Mail Fox News Google KTLA Leftist Influencers MSN MSNBC NBC News New Jersey Monitor People Politico Reuters Scripps Spectrum The BBC The Boston Globe The Bulwark The Daily Beast The Daily Signal The Free Press The Hill The Independent The Los Angeles Times The New York Times The Pulitzer Board The Wall Street Journal The Washington Post TMZ USA Today Wisconsin Public Radio (WPR)\n\n* #### Pulitzer Board Hands Out Once-Prestigious Prize to Anti-Trump Journalists\n\n  The Pulitzer Board\n* #### Journalists Snub Artemis II Astronauts\n* #### MSNBC Depicts WHCD Assassination Attempt As Common Gun Violence\n\n  MSNBC\n* #### ABC Journo Invents Bizarre Lie About President Trump\n\n  ABC News\n* #### TMZ Omits Vital Context About Violent Illegal Alien\n\n  TMZ\n* #### Co-Host Of The View Suggested Pro Athlete Be Injured For Participating In Event With President Trump\n\n  ABC News\n* #### Fox News Holds Softball Interview With Spokesman For Murderous Communist Regime\n\n  Fox News\n* #### CNN Used “Doctor” Who Donated To Cognitively Impaired Joe Biden As “Expert” On Presidential Health\n\n  CNN\n* #### Stephen Colbert Leaves a Legacy of Leftist Lunacy\n\n  CBS News\n* #### News aggregators disproportionately promote left-wing outlets\n\n  Apple News, Google, MSN\n\n## The Leaderboard\n\nA race to the bottom.\n\n## Repeat Offenders\n\nThese outlets don’t just get it wrong – they do it over and over again.\n\n## Report Bias","author":null,"published_date":"2025-11-28T22:19:43+00:00","latency_ms":342.2098539886065,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}